traight. Use createVector with vectorPaths — plugin supports `vectorPaths` via `createVector().vectorPaths = [...]`? Setting vectorPaths requires... In Plugin API, VectorNode.vectorPaths is settable (since API v1.47?) Actually `vectorPaths` is readonly; you set via `vectorNetwork`? There's `figma.createVector()` then `vector.vectorPaths = [{windingRule:'NONE', data:'M ...'}]`? I believe `vectorPaths` IS writable on VectorNode (used widely). Hmm, VectorPathsMixin? Not sure. Safer: skip ECG.\n  | Steps (white, icon, \"Steps\", \"999/2000\" value, progress bar 999/2000≈50%).\n  Row3 y496: Sleep (charcoal tile: moon icon lime, \"Sleep\" white70, bar chart 7 lime bars heights varied + maybe \"7h\"? no value given — chart only) | Water (white: icon blue, \"Water\", \"6/8 Cups\", 8 cup dots/bars with 6 filled blue).\n  Row4 y618: Cycling wide tile 350×150: map photo fill (rounded), overlay bottom gradient charcoal, Icon_Cycling in lime circle top-left, text \"Cycling\" white? and \"Keep it Up! 💪\" 14 Bold white at bottom-left. \n- Tab bar y = 618+150+24 = 792 → frame 792+84=876? Wait we also need spacing: content ends 768, +24 = 792 tab → frame h 876. Nice, close to 844 but slightly over — fine, or compress tiles to 104: rows y252,368,484, cycling y600 h150 → 750, tab 774, frame 858. Eh — I'll compute in code, aim ~1000 with comfortable spacing. Let me give tiles h 120 for breathing room: rows y252,384,516; cycling y648 h160 → 808; tab y 832; frame 916. Good.\n\nStatus bar glyph colors: default black (light screens OK). On 01 photo + 04 hero: override to white.\n\nHome indicator: black pill default; on dark screens override to white. 01 bottom is white bg → keep black. 04 bottom white → black.\n\nPrototype reactions: set on:\n- 01: button instance (root) → 02.\n- 02: popular card instance #1 (Lower Body) → 04; tab bar nested: Home tab item (no link), Explore tab item → 03, Analytics → 05, Profile none. Tab items inside Tab Bar instance are nested instance children — can I set reactions on them? I'll test; else overlay hotspot rects (transparent fills? reactions need the node visible; use fill opacity 0.001? Use fill with 0 opacity? A rectangle with fills=[] can't be clicked? In Figma prototyping, transparent rectangles still receive clicks if they have a fill (even 0% opacity fill). Use solid fill white with opacity 0? Node.opacity=0 might disable hit? Use fill with 0.01 alpha → practically invisible. I'll test reactions on nested children first.)\n\nReactions API: node.reactions = [{ trigger: {type:'ON_CLICK'}, actions: [{type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition: {type:'SMART_ANIMATE', easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}, duration:0.3}, ...}] }]. Actually action structure: {type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition, preserveScrollPosition:false, overlayRelativePosition:null?}. Keep minimal: {trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}, actions:[{type:'NODE', destinationId: X, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:{type:'DISSOLVE',duration:0.2,easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}}]}.\n\nAlright, also nested instance swaps: when I create PlanRow instances and need different photos: rowInstance.children → find photo instance node → swapInstance(photoComp). Allowed (nested swap is an override). ✓. Text overrides: find text nodes by name → set characters (need font loaded ✓).\n\nLevel tag swap: rowInstance nested LevelTag instance → set componentProperties? Variant switch via swapInstance to other variant — variants are components in a set; swapInstance(variantComp) works? For variant sets, recommended: instance.swapComponent(otherVariantNode)? Hmm, for variants you set instance.componentProperties = {Variant: 'Beginner'}? componentProperties property names like \"Variant#1:0\"... messy. Alternative: skip variant set; create 3 separate components LevelTag/Beginner etc. Simpler with swapInstance. But \"component reuse/system\" — variants are nicer. I can still create a variant set via combineAsVariants([...]) then switch by setting componentProperties — property name would be like \"Level\" with values. Setting: instance.componentProperties = {'Level': 'Beginner'}? The actual key includes '#'-suffix? For variant components, componentProperties keys are like \"Property 1#1234:0\". You can read instance.componentProperties to get exact keys, then set. Doable: after creating instance, read keys, set value. I'll implement helper: setVariant(inst, value) that finds key containing 'level' (case-insens) or the only key, and sets it.\n\nOK let me also handle: creating variant set requires components in same parent (page ok) then figma.combineAsVariants(components, page). Then rename property to \"level\". Variant component names \"level=Beginner\" etc.\n\nFor TabBar variants current=Home/Explore/Analytics similarly.\n\nGiven the complexity, I'll write careful code. Let me also double-check emoji rendering: \"Good Morning 🔥\" and \"Keep it Up! 💪\" — Lato has no emoji glyphs; Figma falls back to Apple Color Emoji — must load that font too? For text with emoji, Figma requires fonts for all characters; it uses \"Apple Color Emoji\" font family automatically; when setting characters via API after loadAsync(Lato), missing glyphs may error? Figma loadFontAsync must cover all characters in the string; emoji chars need 'Apple Color Emoji' loaded. Safe: load both Lato styles + 'Apple Color Emoji' (family \"Apple Color Emoji\", style \"Regular\"). If load fails, catch and continue (text might still set with hasMissingFont). I'll try/catch.\n\nLet me start building. Step A: create components batch 1 (tags, chips, day cells, stat chip, challenge card).\n\nComponent coordinates: place at x -1200 .. -500 region, y 0.. each offset. Actually combineAsVariants requires the components; after combining they become a set frame.\n\nLet me define helper functions to include in every call:\n\n```js\nconst WS = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('7:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(WS);\nconst F = async () => { await figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Lato',style:'Regular'}); await figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Lato',style:'Bold'}); await figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Lato',style:'Black'}); try{ await figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Apple Color Emoji',style:'Regular'});}catch(e){} };\nconst C = hex => { const n = parseInt(hex.slice(1),16); return {r:((n>>16)&255)/255, g:((n>>8)&255)/255, b:(n&255)/255}; };\nfunction rect(w,h,color,r){ const n=figma.createRectangle(); n.resize(w,h); if(color) n.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:C(color)}]; if(r!==undefined) n.cornerRadius=r; return n; }\nasync function txt(chars, size, style, color, opts={}){ const t=figma.createText(); t.fontName={family:'Lato',style}; t.characters=chars; t.fontSize=size; t.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:C(color)}]; if(opts.lh) t.lineHeight={value:opts.lh,unit:'PIXELS'}; if(opts.align) t.textAlignHorizontal=opts.align; if(opts.w){t.textAutoResize='HEIGHT'; t.resize(opts.w, t.height);} return t; }\n```\n\nIcon instance helper: \n```js\nasync function icon(name, size, color){ const map={...iconIds}; const comp = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(map[name]); const i = comp.createInstance(); if(size!==24) i.resize(size,size); if(color){ const paint=[{type:'SOLID',color:C(color)}]; i.fills=[]; const set=(n)=>{ if('fills' in n){ try{n.fills=paint;}catch(e){} } (n.children||[]).forEach(set); }; set(i);} return i; }\n```\nWait icon comp root fills white, vectors colored — set all fills to color. Careful: Icon_Back might have transparent parts? Setting all vector fills to color is fine for line icons (they're single-color glyphs; white root fill — should I clear root fills? The component root has white fill (probably invisible backdrop). If I set root white fill to color, a white square appears. So: set root fills = [] (transparent), then children vectors → color. Let me check icon structure: iconFire root fills white + 2 vector children. Are the vectors the flame shape? Probably yes (fill rule evenodd maybe). Set root fills=[] and vector fills=color. ✓ (verified ch