ects=[{type:'DROP_SHADOW',color:{r:0.06,g:0.08,b:0.1,a:0.08},offset:{x:0,y:-4},radius:20,spread:0,visible:true,blendMode:'NORMAL'}];\n  const tabs=[['Home','Home'],['Explore','Explore'],['Analytics','Analytics'],['Profile','Profile']];\n  for(let i=0;i<4;i++){\n    const [nm,icn]=tabs[i];\n    const item=figma.createFrame(); item.name='tab/'+nm; item.resize(97.5,50); item.x=i*97.5; item.y=4; item.fills=[];\n    const active = nm===current;\n    let iconY=6;\n    if(active){ const pill=rect(52,30,'#BBF246',15); pill.x=(97.5-52)/2; pill.y=4; item.appendChild(pill); }\n    const ic=await icon(icn,20, active?'#192126':'#9AA5AE'); ic.x=(97.5-20)/2; ic.y= active? 4+5 : 5; item.appendChild(ic);\n    const lb=txt(nm,10, active?'Black':'Regular', active?'#192126':'#9AA5AE'); lb.x=(97.5-lb.width)/2; lb.y=36; item.appendChild(lb);\n    comp.appendChild(item);\n  }\n  const hi=(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('1:49')).createInstance(); hi.x=0; hi.y=50; comp.appendChild(hi);\n  return comp;\n}\n```\nWait home indicator h34 at y50 → 50+34=84 ✓.\n\ncombineAsVariants for tabbar set name 'Tab Bar'.\n\nPositioning of components on page: I'll set x/y when creating: give each a position in components zone: start x=-1000, stack. Or create a big frame \"⬢ Components\"? Components inside a frame fine. Simpler: absolute positions on page at y -800 (above screens)? Negative coords fine. Zone: x from -1400. Let me place: tags row at (-1400,0); etc. combineAsVariants reparents into set at their location. OK just assign increasing positions.\n\nAfter Batch A/B, return IDs/names.\n\nThen screens. Screen frames: names exactly: \"01_Onboarding\", \"02_Home\", \"03_Explore\", \"04_Workout\", \"05_Analytics\". Positions: 01 at (0,0), 02 at (490,0), 03 at (980,0), 04 at (1470,0), 05 at (1960,0). Heights vary.\n\nComponents zone: x -1600..-500, y 0..  Let me lay: \n- Tag set at (-1600, 0)\n- DayCell set at (-1600, 60)\n- ProgressBar set at (-1600, 150)\n- Stat Chip (-1600, 200)\n- Challenge Card (-1600,